.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the runtime library shared by
.Xr capsule 8 ,
.Xr switchboard 8 ,
.Xr libservice 3 ,
.Xr libcapbundle 3 ,
the capability-plane daemons, and their control tools.
It carries three things: the canonical claim types and constants every
peer agrees on, the UCL claim parsers that turn a Capsule configuration
or a switchboard manifest into those types, and the wire-protocol
headers for each channel protocol of the capability plane.
.Pp
Every wire protocol below is spoken over a
.Xr mac_capability 4
channel using
.Xr libchannel 3
request/reply messages: the first four bytes of a request payload are
the operation code, a reply begins with a
.Vt int32_t
status that is zero on success or a positive
.Xr errno 2
value, and any descriptor a reply delivers rides as an attached
.Dv SCM_RIGHTS
descriptor, never as an integer in the payload.
The headers are built and run together with their peers; a protocol
version bump is a
.Dq rebuild every peer
marker, not a negotiated compatibility knob.
.Ss Shared constants and types
.In capsulert.h
defines the canonical claim descriptors.
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Vt struct ort_net_claim
A network claim:
.Va domain
.Pq Dv AF_INET , AF_INET6 , 0 No for any ,
.Va protocol
.Pq Dv IPPROTO_TCP , IPPROTO_UDP , No a Dv ORT_BTPROTO_* No value, 0 for any ,
.Va port_min
and
.Va port_max
in host byte order,
.Va direction
.Pq Dv ORT_NET_DIR_BIND , ORT_NET_DIR_CONNECT , ORT_NET_DIR_ANY ,
.Va prefix
(CIDR length, 0 for exact or any) and a 16-byte
.Va addr
holding an IPv6 or v4-mapped address, all zero for any.
The layout matches the kernel-side
.Pa mac_capability_isolation_proto.h .
.It Vt struct ort_vsock_claim
A VM-socket claim:
.Va cid
.Pq Dv VSOCK_CID_ANY No or a specific CID ,
a
.Va port_min Ns / Ns Va port_max
range and an
.Dv ORT_NET_DIR_*
.Va direction .
.It Dv ORT_BTPROTO_HCI , ORT_BTPROTO_L2CAP , ORT_BTPROTO_RFCOMM , ORT_BTPROTO_SCO , ORT_BTPROTO_ISO
Stable
.Dv AF_BLUETOOTH
socket protocol numbers (134 through 138) usable in
.Va protocol .
.It Dv ORT_STORAGE_PERSISTENT , ORT_STORAGE_CACHE , ORT_STORAGE_BOOT , ORT_STORAGE_LEASE
Storage lifetimes (0 through 3), numerically identical to the
.Dv BSDFILESYSTEM_*
wire lifetimes.
.Dv ORT_STORAGE_DATASET_MAX
is the opaque ZFS leaf-key width shared with that protocol.
.El
.Pp
.Fn ort_net_domain_name ,
.Fn ort_net_direction_name
and
.Fn ort_net_protocol_name
are inline helpers returning a constant display name
.Pq Dq inet , Dq bind , Dq tcp , ...
for a claim field, or
.Dq any
for an unrecognized or wildcard value.
.Pp
.In mac_capability_versions.h
defines the
.Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_VERSION_*
constants (core, channel, coalition, isolation, system, capprotect,
node, accounting, identity, mount) that
.Xr capsule 8
compares at startup against the loaded
.Xr mac_capability 4
modules to detect a partial upgrade.
.Ss UCL claim parsers
.In claim_parse.h
declares the parsers shared by the Capsule configuration reader and
the switchboard manifest reader.
The
.Vt struct ucl_object_s
argument is a
libucl
object; the header forward-declares it so callers need not include
.In ucl.h .
Every parser returns 0 on success and \-1 on a malformed or
unrecognized input.
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fn parse_port_range_string
Parses
.Dq * ,
a single port, a
.Dq lo-hi
range, or
.Dq .N
and
.Dq <N
(all ports below N) into
.Fa minp
and
.Fa maxp .
.It Fn parse_port_range_obj
Accepts a UCL integer (0 meaning any port) or a string in the form
above.
A
.Dv NULL
object is accepted and leaves the outputs untouched.
.It Fn parse_address_string
Parses
.Dq * ,
an IPv4 or IPv6 literal, or a
.Dq addr/prefix
CIDR form into the 16-byte v4-mapped or IPv6
.Fa addr ,
the prefix length
.Pq 32 or 128 for a bare host
and the address family in
.Fa domainp
.Pq 0 for the wildcard .
.It Fn parse_net_protocol_string
Maps
.Dq tcp ,
.Dq udp ,
.Dq l2cap ,
.Dq rfcomm ,
.Dq sco ,
.Dq iso ,
.Dq hci ,
or
.Dq * Ns / Ns Dq any
to the numeric protocol.
.It Fn parse_bdaddr_string
Parses
.Dq *
or a
.Dq aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff
Bluetooth device address into
.Fa addr
in
.Xr bt_aton 3
byte order with prefix 48, so the claim compares equal to the
.Dv BD_ADDR
the kernel reads from a bind or connect sockaddr.
.It Fn parse_jail_action_string , Fn parse_jail_actions
OR the
.Dv FI_JAIL_*
bit for
.Dq create ,
.Dq get ,
.Dq set ,
.Dq remove ,
.Dq attach
or
.Dq all Ns / Ns Dq *
into
.Fa actionsp .
The object form accepts a string or an array of strings; a
.Dv NULL
object means
.Dv FI_JAIL_ALL
and an empty result is an error.
.It Fn parse_file_action_string , Fn parse_file_actions
The same for the
.Dv FI_FS_*
file actions:
.Dq lookup ,
.Dq stat ,
.Dq read ,
.Dq write ,
.Dq append ,
.Dq create ,
.Dq delete ,
.Dq rename_from ,
.Dq rename_to ,
.Dq link ,
.Dq exec ,
.Dq setattr ,
.Dq truncate ,
.Dq connect
and
.Dq all .
.It Fn parse_storage_right_string , Fn parse_storage_rights
The same for the TrustedZFS
.Dv ZH_*
handle rights of
.In sys/zfshandle.h :
.Dq props_read ,
.Dq props_write ,
.Dq snapshot ,
.Dq snap_destroy ,
.Dq rollback ,
.Dq clone_src ,
.Dq create ,
.Dq destroy ,
.Dq send ,
.Dq recv ,
.Dq mount ,
.Dq hold
and
.Dq all .
Unlike the action parsers, a storage claim must name its rights: a
.Dv NULL
object is an error.
.It Fn parse_storage_lifetime_string
Maps
.Dq persistent
.Pq also Dv NULL ,
.Dq cache ,
.Dq boot
or
.Dq lease
to the
.Dv ORT_STORAGE_*
lifetime.
.El
.Ss Capsule control protocol
.In capsule_ctl.h
is the one-shot request/reply protocol
.Xr capsulectl 8
presents to
.Xr capsule 8 :
a
.Vt struct ctl_request
.Pq Va version , op , flags , datalen
optionally followed by
.Va datalen
payload bytes, answered by a
.Vt struct ctl_reply
.Pq Va status , flags , uptime_usec .
.Dv CTL_VERSION
is 1.
Opcodes:
.Bl -tag -width CTL_OP_POWERCYCLE -compact
.It Dv CTL_OP_SHUTDOWN
graceful daemon shutdown (root).
.It Dv CTL_OP_STATUS
query daemon status (any caller).
.It Dv CTL_OP_RELOAD
reload the configuration claims (root).
.It Dv CTL_OP_REBOOT
reboot
.Pq Dv RB_AUTOBOOT .
.It Dv CTL_OP_HALT
halt.
.It Dv CTL_OP_POWEROFF
halt and power off.
.It Dv CTL_OP_POWERCYCLE
power-cycle.
.It Dv CTL_OP_SINGLE
shut down to single-user mode.
.It Dv CTL_OP_REROOT
re-root the root file system.
.It Dv CTL_OP_RESCAN
re-read
.Pa /etc/ttys
(formerly
.Dv SIGHUP ) .
.It Dv CTL_OP_CATATONIA
stop new logins (formerly
.Dv SIGTSTP ) .
.El
The lifecycle opcodes (4 through 14) are the replacement for the
traditional
.Xr init 8
signal ABI, are valid only when Capsule is PID 1 and require root.
Opcodes 7 through 9 are reserved and must not be reused.
Today these opcodes travel inside a
.Dv CAPSULE_OP_LIFECYCLE
request relayed by switchboard (below); the original control socket
has been retired.
.Ss Capsule service protocol
.In capsule_svc_proto.h
is the protocol between
.Xr switchboard 8
and
.Xr capsule 8
over the channel switchboard inherits as descriptor 3.
All requests originate from switchboard; Capsule only replies with a
.Vt struct capsule_reply
.Pq Va status
plus at most
.Dv CAPSULE_MAX_REPLY_FDS
(2) descriptors.
.Bl -tag -width CAPSULE_OP_SET_AMBIENT_LOOKUP -compact
.It Dv CAPSULE_OP_MINT_NET
mint a network isolation token from a
.Vt struct capsule_net_req
(same fields as
.Vt struct ort_net_claim ) ;
returns the token descriptor.
.It Dv CAPSULE_OP_MINT_VSOCK
mint a VM-socket isolation token from a
.Vt struct capsule_vsock_req .
.It Dv CAPSULE_OP_MINT_SYSTEM
mint a system-gate token for the
.Dv SYS_GATE_*
mask in
.Vt struct capsule_system_req ;
an optional opaque
.Vt sys_sysctl_oidset
trailer (valid only with
.Dv SYS_GATE_SYSCTL )
scopes a per-OID sysctl claim.
.It Dv CAPSULE_OP_CLAIM_NET , CAPSULE_OP_CLAIM_VSOCK , CAPSULE_OP_CLAIM_SYSTEM
dynamically add a reference-counted claim to Capsule's claimed set
without minting.
.It Dv CAPSULE_OP_RELEASE_NET , CAPSULE_OP_RELEASE_VSOCK , CAPSULE_OP_RELEASE_SYSTEM
drop a dynamic claim
.Pq Er ENOENT No if absent , Er EPERM No for a policy claim .
.It Dv CAPSULE_OP_CREATE_CHANNEL
create a restricted channel pair; returns both endpoints.
.It Dv CAPSULE_OP_CREATE_COALITION
create a coalition; returns its instance descriptor.
.It Dv CAPSULE_OP_DELEGATE_SERVICE
delegate the named capability-service instance in
.Vt struct capsule_service_req .
.It Dv CAPSULE_OP_READY
switchboard reports that its inherited descriptors are confined and
its capprotect shield is active.
.It Dv CAPSULE_OP_PING
liveness check.
.It Dv CAPSULE_OP_SET_AMBIENT_LOOKUP
hand Capsule a duplicate of the SYSTEM ambient lookup channel so
getty/login sessions inherit it at the fixed descriptor; best effort.
.It Dv CAPSULE_OP_LIFECYCLE
apply the
.Dv CTL_OP_*
transition in
.Vt struct capsule_lifecycle_req .
.It Dv CAPSULE_OP_RELOAD
reload the Capsule configuration claims.
.El
Mint operations implicitly claim any resource not already held.
Opcodes 1, 8, 9, 10, 11, 13, 15, 17, 22, 24 and 25 are retired: path,
file and storage brokering moved to
.Xr BSDFilesystem 8 ,
jails to
.Xr BSDNamespace 8
and kernel-module loading to
.Xr BSDExtension 8 .
The
.Dv BUF_APPEND
macro is a bounded
.Xr snprintf 3
accumulator shared by the two daemons' status formatters.
.Ss Switchboard control protocol
.In switchboard_ctl.h
is the request/reply protocol
.Xr switchboardctl 8
and
.Xr capsulectl 8
speak over the ADMIN-bearing channels switchboard serves under
.Dv SWITCHBOARD_CONTROL_NAME
.Pq Dq system.switchboard
and
.Dv SWITCHBOARD_LIFECYCLE_NAME
.Pq Dq system.lifecycle .
A
.Vt struct sctl_request
.Pq Va version , op , flags , datalen
is answered by a
.Vt struct sctl_reply
whose
.Va flags
carries the length of the summary text that follows.
.Dv SWITCHBOARD_CTL_VERSION
is 2.
.Bl -tag -width SCTL_OP_START_SVC -compact
.It Dv SCTL_OP_STATUS
query switchboard status.
.It Dv SCTL_OP_SERVICES
list loaded units.
.It Dv SCTL_OP_RELOAD
reload manifests (ADMIN).
.It Dv SCTL_OP_START_SVC
start a loaded unit (ADMIN).
.It Dv SCTL_OP_STOP_SVC
stop a loaded unit (ADMIN).
.El
.Ss Switchboard service protocol
.In switchboard_svc_proto.h
is the protocol between a launched unit and
.Xr switchboard 8
over the unit's inherited channel (descriptor 3), and between any
process and switchboard over an ambient lookup channel.
.Xr libservice 3
implements it; services do not normally speak it directly.
.Dv SWITCHBOARD_SVC_PROTO_VERSION
is 15.
Requests carry a
.Vt struct svc_reply
.Pq Va status
answer.
Service to switchboard:
.Bl -tag -width SVC_OP_REGISTER_LOOKUP -compact
.It Dv SVC_OP_NAME_CLAIM
check in one listener for a manifest-reserved
.Va provides[]
name
.Pq Vt struct svc_name_claim_req ;
.Dv SVC_NAME_CLAIM_SENDABLE
leaves delivered client endpoints re-sendable.
.It Dv SVC_OP_READY
readiness advisory; every declared name must already be claimed.
.It Dv SVC_OP_NAME_RESULT
complete a preceding
.Dv SVC_OP_ACTIVATE_NAME
with 0 or an errno
.Pq Vt struct svc_name_result_req .
.It Dv SVC_OP_NAME_WITHDRAW
stop serving one claimed name.
.It Dv SVC_OP_LOOKUP
connect to a named service
.Pq Vt struct svc_lookup_req ;
the reply attaches the caller's channel endpoint.
.It Dv SVC_OP_QUIESCE_RESULT
report completion of a managed shutdown.
.It Dv SVC_OP_WORKER_CHANNEL
create an unnamed provider/worker channel pair; returns both ends.
.It Dv SVC_OP_IDLE
request idle-timeout shutdown after
.Va seconds
of no demand (0 cancels).
.It Dv SVC_OP_MINT_DOMAIN
mint a narrowed lookup channel for a session
.Pq Vt struct svc_mint_domain_req :
.Dv SVC_MINT_DOMAIN_USER
(per-uid),
.Dv SVC_MINT_DOMAIN_SYSTEM
or
.Dv SVC_MINT_DOMAIN_CONTROL ,
with the
.Dv SVC_MINT_FLAG_RESEND ,
.Dv SVC_MINT_FLAG_ANOINT_ALL
and
.Dv SVC_MINT_FLAG_ADMIN_RIGHTS
flags and an anointment set of up to
.Dv SVC_ANOINT_MAX
names; only a SYSTEM caller may mint.
.It Dv SVC_OP_AMBIENT_HELLO
behavioral probe answered with
.Dv SVC_AMBIENT_HELLO_MAGIC
only by a genuine lookup channel.
.It Dv SVC_OP_HELPER_OPEN
launch and connect a bundle-local private helper unit
.Pq Vt struct svc_helper_req .
.It Dv SVC_OP_HEARTBEAT
liveness ping that re-arms the manifest
.Va watchdog
timer.
.It Dv SVC_OP_REGISTER_LOOKUP
adopt a caller-created private lookup channel; acknowledged with a
.Vt struct svc_register_lookup_ack
pushed on the adopted channel.
.El
Switchboard to service (events):
.Bl -tag -width SVC_OP_ACTIVATE_NAME -compact
.It Dv SVC_OP_ACTIVATE_NAME
initialize one reserved name
.Pq Vt struct svc_activate_name_msg .
.It Dv SVC_OP_NEW_CLIENT
a new client session
.Pq Vt struct svc_new_client_msg
with the client's channel endpoint attached; carries the client's
label, bundle container, group containers, per-exec nonce, ABI
.Pq Dv SVC_CLIENT_ABI_*
and granted
.Va rights
.Pq Dv SVC_RIGHTS_ALL , SVC_RIGHTS_ADMIN .
.It Dv SVC_OP_QUIESCE
stop admission and drain within
.Va deadline_ms
for reason
.Dv SVC_QUIESCE_REASON_STOP ,
.Dv SVC_QUIESCE_REASON_SHUTDOWN
or
.Dv SVC_QUIESCE_REASON_RELOAD .
.El
.Ss BSDFilesystem protocol
.In bsdfilesystem_proto.h
is the storage protocol of
.Xr BSDFilesystem 8 ,
reached by opening
.Dv BSDFILESYSTEM_SERVICE_NAME
.Pq Dq system.Filesystem .
Every claim is resolved under the caller's own container, derived from
the connecting channel's unforgeable label, so a caller can never name
another label's storage.
.Dv BSDFILESYSTEM_PROTO_VERSION
is 6.
Requests are a
.Vt struct bsdfilesystem_request
.Pq Va rights , quota , lifetime , deliver , scope , dataset , group , ...
unless noted, answered by a
.Vt struct bsdfilesystem_reply
.Pq Va status , dataset .
.Bl -tag -width BSDFILESYSTEM_OP_LIST_VERSIONS -compact
.It Dv BSDFILESYSTEM_OP_REQUEST
mint a storage handle for a dataset claim; delivers the TrustedZFS
handle
.Pq Dv BSDFILESYSTEM_DELIVER_HANDLE ,
a mounted directory
.Pq Dv BSDFILESYSTEM_DELIVER_MOUNTED
or a read-only view
.Pq Dv BSDFILESYSTEM_DELIVER_MOUNTED_RO
in scope
.Dv BSDFILESYSTEM_SCOPE_UNIT ,
.Dv BSDFILESYSTEM_SCOPE_SHARED
or
.Dv BSDFILESYSTEM_SCOPE_GROUP .
.It Dv BSDFILESYSTEM_OP_RELEASE
tear down a lease claim (idempotent).
.It Dv BSDFILESYSTEM_OP_PING
liveness check.
.It Dv BSDFILESYSTEM_OP_BEGIN_SESSION
select or reconcile the caller's lease generation.
.It Dv BSDFILESYSTEM_OP_OPEN
open an existing path on the caller's behalf
.Pq Vt struct bsdfilesystem_open_request
under the daemon's per-label policy and return a descriptor limited to
the
.Dv BSDFILESYSTEM_OPEN_*
rights.
.It Dv BSDFILESYSTEM_OP_DESTROY
reclaim a persistent or cache claim
.Pq Er ENOENT No if absent .
.It Dv BSDFILESYSTEM_OP_LIST
page the caller's own claims of one scope
.Pq Vt struct bsdfilesystem_list_request Ns / Ns Vt bsdfilesystem_list_reply ,
.Dv BSDFILESYSTEM_LIST_MAX
entries per page.
.It Dv BSDFILESYSTEM_OP_STAT_CLAIM
report one claim's usage, refquota and available bytes
.Pq Vt struct bsdfilesystem_stat_reply .
.It Dv BSDFILESYSTEM_OP_SET_QUOTA
raise, lower or clear a claim's refquota.
.It Dv BSDFILESYSTEM_OP_SNAPSHOT
snapshot a claim; returns the assigned version id
.Pq Vt struct bsdfilesystem_version_reply .
.It Dv BSDFILESYSTEM_OP_LIST_VERSIONS
page a claim's version ids
.Pq Vt struct bsdfilesystem_versions_reply .
.It Dv BSDFILESYSTEM_OP_ROLLBACK
roll a claim back to a version (destructive).
.It Dv BSDFILESYSTEM_OP_OPEN_VERSION
mount a version read-only into the caller's lease namespace and return
the directory descriptor.
.It Dv BSDFILESYSTEM_OP_TXN_BEGIN
clone a claim into a writable staging dataset; returns the txn id and
its directory descriptor.
.It Dv BSDFILESYSTEM_OP_TXN_COMMIT
atomically swap the staging clone in as the claim.
.It Dv BSDFILESYSTEM_OP_TXN_ABORT
discard the staging clone.
.It Dv BSDFILESYSTEM_OP_UNMOUNT
drop the caller's claim mount anchor.
.El
The version and transaction operations share
.Vt struct bsdfilesystem_version_request .
Opcode 3 is unassigned.
.Ss BSDNamespace protocol
.In bsdnamespace_proto.h
is the jail protocol of
.Xr BSDNamespace 8 ,
reached by opening
.Dv BSDNAMESPACE_SERVICE_NAME
.Pq Dq system.Namespace .
A label owns at most one jail, named by the daemon from the channel
label.
.Bl -tag -width BSDNAMESPACE_OP_DESTROY_JAIL -compact
.It Dv BSDNAMESPACE_OP_ENTER_JAIL
create or reuse the caller's jail from a
.Vt struct bsdnamespace_request
.Pq Va path , hostname , ip4_addr , ip6_addr , flags
and return the non-owning jail descriptor the caller attaches itself
to.
.Dv BSDNAMESPACE_F_EPHEMERAL
binds the jail's lifetime to the connection;
.Dv BSDNAMESPACE_F_VNET
gives it its own network stack.
.It Dv BSDNAMESPACE_OP_DESTROY_JAIL
remove the caller's jail
.Pq Vt struct bsdnamespace_control_request ;
.Er ENOENT
if none.
.It Dv BSDNAMESPACE_OP_LIST_JAILS
report the caller's jail definition in a
.Vt struct bsdnamespace_list_reply
.Pq Va present , jid , flags , path , ... .
.El
.Ss BSDExtension protocol
.In sysext_proto.h
is the kernel-module protocol of
.Xr BSDExtension 8 ,
reached by opening
.Dv SYSEXT_SERVICE_NAME
.Pq Dq system.SystemExtension .
Requests are a
.Vt struct sysext_request
.Pq Va op , name .
.Bl -tag -width SYSEXT_OP_RELOAD -compact
.It Dv SYSEXT_OP_ENSURE
load the named module if it is not already loaded
.Pq Vt struct sysext_reply .
.It Dv SYSEXT_OP_STAT
query whether it is loaded without loading
.Pq Vt struct sysext_stat_reply .
.It Dv SYSEXT_OP_LIST
return the allow-listed module names, at most
.Dv SYSEXT_LIST_MAX
.Pq Vt struct sysext_list_reply .
.It Dv SYSEXT_OP_RELOAD
reload the configured policy file (ADMIN).
.El
A name outside the allow-list fails
.Er EPERM
for both
.Dv ENSURE
and
.Dv STAT ;
there is deliberately no unload operation.
.Ss BSDVM protocol
.In bsdvm_proto.h
(renamed from
.Pa vmd_proto.h ;
its
.Dv VMD_*
identifiers are the unchanged wire names) is the VM-socket protocol of
.Xr BSDVM 8 ,
reached by opening
.Dv VMD_SERVICE_NAME
.Pq Dq system.VM .
Each label owns an exclusive window of
.Dv VMD_PORTS_PER_LABEL
(16) ports above
.Dv VMD_PORT_BASE
on the host-local CID.
Requests are a 16-byte
.Vt struct vmd_request
.Pq Va op , port , backlog , cid ;
unused fields must be zero.
.Bl -tag -width VMD_OP_VSOCK_CONNECT -compact
.It Dv VMD_OP_VSOCK_BIND
bind and listen on window index
.Va port ;
the
.Vt struct vmd_reply
attaches the listening socket and reports the concrete
.Va cid Ns / Ns Va port
to advertise.
.It Dv VMD_OP_VSOCK_CONNECT
dial a peer's advertised concrete
.Pq Va cid , port
and attach the connected socket.
.It Dv VMD_OP_VSOCK_LIST
report the caller's own window in a
.Vt struct vmd_list_reply
